    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d112">

                <pb facs="0245" n="155" sameAs="frus:frus1875v01/pg155"/>

                <head>No. 108.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Williamson to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation in Central America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1875-02-16"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 16, 1875</date>. (Received March. 11.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 315.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to send you herewith a
                    copy of an interesting dispatch from Mr. Romeo H. Freer, commercial agent at San
                    Juan del Norte.</p>
                <p>It is mainly corroborative of information and suggestions heretofore <pb
                        facs="0246" n="156" xml:id="pg156"/> made, in my dispatches Nos. 269<anchor
                        n="*" xml:id="d112-f1"/> and 289,<anchor n="*" xml:id="d112-f2"/> referring
                    to the same subject; but in the marked passages on pages 5 and 6 you will find
                    more explicit statements than I have been able to make.</p>
                <p>It seems probable that the captain of the British man-of-war and the vice-consul
                    at Greytown were acting with the knowledge, if not under the instructions, of
                    their government.</p>
                <p>The British minister here assures me he has no knowledge of anything that has
                    been done in relation to the Mosquito question, as reported by Mr. Freer, and I
                    believe he has no instructions on the subject.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GEO. WILLIAMSON.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d112-a1.xml" xpointer="d112-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
